            Five of the eight list 0 g of sugar. The other three, Quest, NOW and ISO100, carry under 1 g to about 1 g, which is nutritionally trivial but technically above the threshold for a sugar-free claim. We included them because many readers searching for sugar-free protein really want "as close to zero as possible with a good flavor", and these three deliver that. If you need the strict definition, stick to the first five rows.
          </p>

          <p>
            Isopure Zero Carb is our overall pick: 0 g of sugar, about 25 g of protein and no sugar alcohols. Naked Whey Isolate is the choice for people who want no sweeteners at all, OWYN Pro Elite is the sugar-free vegan option, and Garden of Life Raw Organic suits people who want organic and fiber and tolerate erythritol. If carbohydrate matters as much as sugar, our <a href="/best-low-carb-protein-powder/">best low carb protein powder</a> guide ranks powders on total carbs.
          </p>
        </div>

