            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>What does sugar free mean on a protein powder label?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Under FDA rules, sugar free, zero sugar or no sugar means less than 0.5 g of sugars per serving and no sugar ingredients unless marked as trivial. If the product is not also low or reduced in calories, it must say so, for example not for weight control. A 0 g panel figure can mean anything under 0.5 g.
                </p>
