            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is no added sugar the same as sugar free?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  No. No added sugar means no sugars were added during processing, but natural sugars such as lactose can remain. A whey concentrate labeled no added sugar may still contain 2 to 3 g of sugar per scoop. Sugar free requires under 0.5 g of total sugars per serving, whatever the source.
                </p>
